        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ka'Chava is a well-made vegan meal shake with a label that does most of what it promises: 25 g of plant protein, about 240 calories, useful fiber and a broad multivitamin in one scoop of convenience. Its weaknesses are the price, the proprietary blends and the lack of a sport certification. Buy chocolate first if you want it as breakfast, vanilla if you blend or drink it daily.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If protein is the goal, skip it and buy a plain plant protein for a fraction of the cost per 25 g. If you want a heavier meal shake, Huel Black Edition gives more protein per serving. Either way, compare cost per serving, not bag price, and try the texture before you subscribe.
          </p>
